    ('8c7d04dc-f567-4759-b99b-0ae8f26d6f32'::uuid, 'd1792200-1d3b-4955-a0b7-0e6980d7a7b2'::uuid, '86d893a1-c1a2-4bbf-b4e5-69ec43221194'::uuid, '2a18c152-67a0-4380-a381-cb8795110a7c'::uuid, 'Blanked 2026-10-07, and ⚠ THE UNDERLYING FINDING IS TRUE -- it is recorded here so it is not lost. Dylan A. Fernandes voted for the VOTES Act -- House roll call #200 (enactment, 06/16/2022), 126-29. The vote was divided (81% yea), so it is distinctive; only the citation was false. The Season 2 rung at this value asks a different question. Season 1: "automatically register all eligible citizens to vote and allow online voting" Season 2: "Require no identification to vote, verifying voters by signature or existing records." The finding itself stands and is preserved here, but it cannot seat the Season 2 chair, and a repair may not move a chair. (the parse was checked against the roll call''s own declared totals before any name was read off it). 🔴 THE CITED BILL IS NOT THE ACT. The row cites 192/S2294, which is "An Act relative to tolls on the roadways of the Commonwealth". The VOTES Act was filed as S.2545, reprinted as S.2554 and ENACTED AS S.2924, Chapter 92 of the Acts of 2022. 🔴🔴 BUT THE SEASON 2 LADDER ASKS A DIFFERENT QUESTION. The Season 2 rung at this value asks a different question. Season 1: "automatically register all eligible citizens to vote and allow online voting" Season 2: "Require no identification to vote, verifying voters by signature or existing records." Season 1 asked about registration, early voting and mail ballots -- the subject of the VOTES Act. Season 2 asks only about VOTER IDENTIFICATION. A verified vote on the VOTES Act locates nobody on a voter-ID scale, so carrying the chair across would seat this member on a position never assessed. That is the Carson call of migration 1896 and the ladder-scope register. A verified fact with nowhere to sit is still a verified fact: it is written here so the next researcher starts from it rather than from nothing. The sources examined are kept below so the next reader does not re-derive this. This is a blank, not a deletion -- the chair may well be re-researchable, and that is an invitation.', ARRAY['https://malegislature.gov/Bills/192/S2294', 'https://malegislature.gov/Bills/192/S2924', 'https://malegislature.gov/RollCall/192/HouseRollCall200.pdf']::text[]),
  -- Erika Uyterhoeven / healthcare  (Season 1 chair 1 -> 1, COSPONSOR_CONFIRMED)
    ('98291d86-d42d-49d0-a5b2-d689a8154b15'::uuid, 'e8dad4a8-eb93-4931-91f5-d8fb5d7dd529'::uuid, '86d893a1-c1a2-4bbf-b4e5-69ec43221194'::uuid, 'afc91aa2-4d48-4db6-aebd-f4c9788e6ad7'::uuid, 'Citation repaired 2026-10-07 (migration 1900); THE CHAIR IS UNCHANGED. The claim was right and the citation was wrong. 🔴 THE CITED BILL IS NOT THE ACT. The row cites 194/H1279, which is "Resolve creating a special commission on affordable housing insurance". 🔑 THE SPONSORSHIP IS VERIFIED ON THE BILL''S OWN COSPONSORS PAGE: Erika Uyterhoeven is a cosponsor of the Medicare for All Massachusetts Act (192/H1267, 192/S766, 193/H1239, 194/H1405). The claim holds; only the citation was false. ⚠ The search was run across EVERY General Court in which the act has been filed, not only the court the row names: 187/S501, 188/S515, 189/H1026, 189/S579, 190/S619, 191/H1194, 191/S683, 192/H1267, 192/S766, 193/H1239, 193/S744, 194/H1405, 194/H5590, 194/S860. A member who signed an earlier filing is a cosponsor of the act whatever the row cites. The sources now point at the cosponsor list that carries the member''s name.', ARRAY['https://malegislature.gov/Bills/192/H1267/Cosponsor', 'https://malegislature.gov/Bills/192/S766/Cosponsor', 'https://malegislature.gov/Bills/193/H1239/Cosponsor', 'https://malegislature.gov/Bills/194/H1405/Cosponsor']::text[]),
  -- Erika Uyterhoeven / judicial-criminal-justice  (Season 1 chair 1 -> 0, NOT_SERVING)
