    ('869ba820-3138-473c-b70d-383e67f5797d'::uuid, 'af2fdfd6-02c4-49df-b09c-cf8536f4773f'::uuid, '86d893a1-c1a2-4bbf-b4e5-69ec43221194'::uuid, 'dab46e5c-628a-4360-ad1d-3aaba61768f0'::uuid, 'Citation repaired 2026-10-07 (migration 1900); THE CHAIR IS UNCHANGED. The claim was right and the citation was wrong. 🔴 THE CITED BILL IS NOT THE ACT. The row cites 191/H4998, which is "An Act directing the State Retirement Board to grant creditable service to Cheryl A. Bednarik". The ROE Act''s own bill, H.3320 of the 191st, NEVER REACHED A FLOOR VOTE -- "No further action taken", 1/5/2021. The ROE Act became law as H.5179, "An Act providing for access to reproductive health services", enacted as section 40 of the FY21 budget and passed over the Governor''s veto: Chapter 263 of the Acts of 2020. 🔑 THE VOTE IS VERIFIED AGAINST THE PRIMARY RECORD: Jonathan D. Zlotnik voted for the ROE Act -- House roll call #374 (veto override, 12/28/2020), 107-46. The vote was divided (70% yea), so it is distinctive; only the citation was false. (the parse was checked against the roll call''s own declared totals before any name was read off it). 🔑 A near-unanimous vote cannot establish a distinctive position -- the rule that blanked Newhouse on 385-41 in migration 1894 and Dingell on 417-10 in 1896 -- so the margin was checked before the chair was kept, not after. The sources now point at the enacted vehicle and the roll call itself.', ARRAY['https://malegislature.gov/Bills/191/H5179', 'https://malegislature.gov/Legislators/Profile/JDZ1', 'https://malegislature.gov/RollCall/191/HouseRollCall317.pdf', 'https://malegislature.gov/RollCall/191/HouseRollCall374.pdf']::text[]),
  -- Jonathan D. Zlotnik / public-safety-approach  (Season 1 chair 2 -> 2, VOTE_CONFIRMED)
