  -- Mike Connolly / healthcare  (Season 1 chair 1 -> 1, COSPONSOR_CONFIRMED)
    ('49963775-d2d5-4ae2-95cf-b2b8d0ed2a92'::uuid, 'e8dad4a8-eb93-4931-91f5-d8fb5d7dd529'::uuid, '86d893a1-c1a2-4bbf-b4e5-69ec43221194'::uuid, 'afc91aa2-4d48-4db6-aebd-f4c9788e6ad7'::uuid, 'Citation repaired 2026-10-07 (migration 1900); THE CHAIR IS UNCHANGED. The claim was right and the citation was wrong. 🔴 THE CITED BILL IS NOT THE ACT. The row cites 194/H1279, which is "Resolve creating a special commission on affordable housing insurance". 🔑 THE SPONSORSHIP IS VERIFIED ON THE BILL''S OWN COSPONSORS PAGE: Mike Connolly is a cosponsor of the Medicare for All Massachusetts Act (190/S619, 191/H1194, 191/S683, 192/H1267, 193/H1239, 193/S744, 194/H1405, 194/S860). The claim holds; only the citation was false. ⚠ The search was run across EVERY General Court in which the act has been filed, not only the court the row names: 187/S501, 188/S515, 189/H1026, 189/S579, 190/S619, 191/H1194, 191/S683, 192/H1267, 192/S766, 193/H1239, 193/S744, 194/H1405, 194/H5590, 194/S860. A member who signed an earlier filing is a cosponsor of the act whatever the row cites. The sources now point at the cosponsor list that carries the member''s name.', ARRAY['https://malegislature.gov/Bills/190/S619/Cosponsor', 'https://malegislature.gov/Bills/191/H1194/Cosponsor', 'https://malegislature.gov/Bills/191/S683/Cosponsor', 'https://malegislature.gov/Bills/192/H1267/Cosponsor', 'https://malegislature.gov/Bills/193/H1239/Cosponsor', 'https://malegislature.gov/Bills/193/S744/Cosponsor', 'https://malegislature.gov/Bills/194/H1405/Cosponsor', 'https://malegislature.gov/Bills/194/S860/Cosponsor']::text[]),
  -- Mike Connolly / judicial-criminal-justice  (Season 1 chair 1 -> 1, VOTE_CONFIRMED)
    ('49963775-d2d5-4ae2-95cf-b2b8d0ed2a92'::uuid, '9db07b16-1076-4b7d-ad89-ebe7b51f4336'::uuid, '86d893a1-c1a2-4bbf-b4e5-69ec43221194'::uuid, 'c334f475-05bd-48ba-9d25-f4de593a3f15'::uuid, 'Citation repaired 2026-10-07 (migration 1900); THE CHAIR IS UNCHANGED. The claim was right and the citation was wrong. 🔴 THE CITED BILL IS NOT THE ACT. The row cites 191/H4990, which is "An Act authorizing the Town of North Attleborough to issue an additional liquor license". The police reform act was filed as S.2800, reprinted as S.2820 and ENACTED AS S.2963, Chapter 253 of the Acts of 2020. 🔑 THE VOTE IS VERIFIED AGAINST THE PRIMARY RECORD: Mike Connolly voted for the 2020 police reform act -- House roll call #326 (re-enactment, 12/23/2020), 107-51. The vote was divided (68% yea), so it is distinctive; only the citation was false. (the parse was checked against the roll call''s own declared totals before any name was read off it). 🔑 A near-unanimous vote cannot establish a distinctive position -- the rule that blanked Newhouse on 385-41 in migration 1894 and Dingell on 417-10 in 1896 -- so the margin was checked before the chair was kept, not after. The sources now point at the enacted vehicle and the roll call itself.', ARRAY['https://malegislature.gov/Bills/191/S2963', 'https://malegislature.gov/RollCall/191/HouseRollCall285.pdf', 'https://malegislature.gov/RollCall/191/HouseRollCall326.pdf']::text[]),
