  -- Natalie Higgins / voting-rights  (Season 1 chair 1 -> 0, LADDER_SCOPE)
    ('c14b3502-f142-4c1f-bfa9-a8fa52351a8e'::uuid, 'd1792200-1d3b-4955-a0b7-0e6980d7a7b2'::uuid, '86d893a1-c1a2-4bbf-b4e5-69ec43221194'::uuid, '2a18c152-67a0-4380-a381-cb8795110a7c'::uuid, 'Blanked 2026-10-07, and ⚠ THE UNDERLYING FINDING IS TRUE -- it is recorded here so it is not lost. Natalie Higgins voted for the VOTES Act -- House roll call #200 (enactment, 06/16/2022), 126-29. The vote was divided (81% yea), so it is distinctive; only the citation was false. The Season 2 rung at this value asks a different question. Season 1: "automatically register all eligible citizens to vote and allow online voting" Season 2: "Require no identification to vote, verifying voters by signature or existing records." The finding itself stands and is preserved here, but it cannot seat the Season 2 chair, and a repair may not move a chair. (the parse was checked against the roll call''s own declared totals before any name was read off it). 🔴 THE CITED BILL IS NOT THE ACT. The row cites 192/H5001, which is "An Act increasing diagnostic testing preparedness". The VOTES Act was filed as S.2545, reprinted as S.2554 and ENACTED AS S.2924, Chapter 92 of the Acts of 2022. 🔴🔴 BUT THE SEASON 2 LADDER ASKS A DIFFERENT QUESTION. The Season 2 rung at this value asks a different question. Season 1: "automatically register all eligible citizens to vote and allow online voting" Season 2: "Require no identification to vote, verifying voters by signature or existing records." Season 1 asked about registration, early voting and mail ballots -- the subject of the VOTES Act. Season 2 asks only about VOTER IDENTIFICATION. A verified vote on the VOTES Act locates nobody on a voter-ID scale, so carrying the chair across would seat this member on a position never assessed. That is the Carson call of migration 1896 and the ladder-scope register. A verified fact with nowhere to sit is still a verified fact: it is written here so the next researcher starts from it rather than from nothing. The sources examined are kept below so the next reader does not re-derive this. This is a blank, not a deletion -- the chair may well be re-researchable, and that is an invitation.', ARRAY['https://malegislature.gov/Bills/192/H5001', 'https://malegislature.gov/Bills/192/S2924', 'https://malegislature.gov/Legislators/Profile/N_H1/Bills', 'https://malegislature.gov/RollCall/192/HouseRollCall200.pdf']::text[]),
  -- Patrick M. O'Connor / voting-rights  (Season 1 chair 4 -> 0, LADDER_SCOPE)
