    ('28a703f8-8316-4d3c-bfc0-3dcd77eab96c'::uuid, 'af2fdfd6-02c4-49df-b09c-cf8536f4773f'::uuid, '86d893a1-c1a2-4bbf-b4e5-69ec43221194'::uuid, 'dab46e5c-628a-4360-ad1d-3aaba61768f0'::uuid, 'Citation repaired 2026-10-07 (migration 1900); THE CHAIR IS UNCHANGED. The claim was right and the citation was wrong. 🔴 THE CITED BILL IS NOT THE ACT. The row cites 194/H1742, which is "An Act to clarify the charitable purposes of certain organizations". 🔑 THE SPONSORSHIP IS VERIFIED ON THE BILL''S OWN COSPONSORS PAGE: Samantha Montaño is a cosponsor of abortion-access legislation (193/H1599, 194/H1815). The claim holds; only the citation was false. ⚠ The search was run across EVERY General Court in which the act has been filed, not only the court the row names: 193/H1599, 193/S1114, 194/H1815, 194/S1244, 194/S1579. A member who signed an earlier filing is a cosponsor of the act whatever the row cites. The sources now point at the cosponsor list that carries the member''s name.', ARRAY['https://malegislature.gov/Bills/193/H1599/Cosponsor', 'https://malegislature.gov/Bills/194/H1815/Cosponsor', 'https://malegislature.gov/Legislators/Profile/S_M1']::text[]),
  -- Samantha Montaño / jail-capacity  (Season 1 chair 1 -> 1, COSPONSOR_CONFIRMED)
    ('28a703f8-8316-4d3c-bfc0-3dcd77eab96c'::uuid, 'c267e137-0ff9-4e7d-9d13-e3cea1756cd0'::uuid, '86d893a1-c1a2-4bbf-b4e5-69ec43221194'::uuid, 'f63a4e70-055e-4115-a5e0-3deeb5748816'::uuid, 'Citation repaired 2026-10-07 (migration 1900); THE CHAIR IS UNCHANGED. The claim was right and the citation was wrong. 🔴 THE CITED BILL IS NOT THE ACT. The row cites 194/H1795, which is "An Act relative to prejudgment interest rates". 🔑 THE SPONSORSHIP IS VERIFIED ON THE BILL''S OWN COSPONSORS PAGE: Samantha Montaño is a cosponsor of the jail and prison construction moratorium (193/H1795, 194/H3422). The claim holds; only the citation was false. ⚠ The search was run across EVERY General Court in which the act has been filed, not only the court the row names: 192/H1905, 192/S2030, 193/H1795, 193/S1979, 193/S2821, 194/H3422, 194/S2114, 194/S2944. A member who signed an earlier filing is a cosponsor of the act whatever the row cites. The sources now point at the cosponsor list that carries the member''s name.', ARRAY['https://malegislature.gov/Bills/193/H1795/Cosponsor', 'https://malegislature.gov/Bills/194/H3422/Cosponsor', 'https://malegislature.gov/Legislators/Profile/S_M1']::text[]),
  -- Samantha Montaño / rent-regulation  (Season 1 chair 2 -> 2, COSPONSOR_CONFIRMED)
    ('28a703f8-8316-4d3c-bfc0-3dcd77eab96c'::uuid, 'c308e8e8-caac-44f5-ab04-dbfecf40bbe2'::uuid, '86d893a1-c1a2-4bbf-b4e5-69ec43221194'::uuid, '6fa44a68-8006-48e9-b562-6b5e61d58693'::uuid, 'Citation repaired 2026-10-07 (migration 1900); THE CHAIR IS UNCHANGED. The claim was right and the citation was wrong. 🔴 THE CITED BILL IS NOT THE ACT. The row cites 194/H1304, which is "An Act relative to the compulsory automobile insurance limits". 🔑 THE SPONSORSHIP IS VERIFIED ON THE BILL''S OWN COSPONSORS PAGE: Samantha Montaño is a cosponsor of rent stabilization legislation (193/H1304, 193/H2103, 194/H2328). The claim holds; only the citation was false. ⚠ The search was run across EVERY General Court in which the act has been filed, not only the court the row names: 191/H3924, 192/H1378, 192/S886, 193/H1304, 193/H2103, 193/S1299, 193/S872, 194/H1477, 194/H2328, 194/S1447. A member who signed an earlier filing is a cosponsor of the act whatever the row cites. The sources now point at the cosponsor list that carries the member''s name.', ARRAY['https://malegislature.gov/Bills/193/H1304/Cosponsor', 'https://malegislature.gov/Bills/193/H2103/Cosponsor', 'https://malegislature.gov/Bills/194/H2328/Cosponsor', 'https://malegislature.gov/Legislators/Profile/S_M1']::text[]),
  -- William F. MacGregor / abortion  (Season 1 chair 2 -> 0, NOT_SERVING)
    ('194b9b91-6986-423e-89a0-ee9750f275d8'::uuid, 'af2fdfd6-02c4-49df-b09c-cf8536f4773f'::uuid, '86d893a1-c1a2-4bbf-b4e5-69ec43221194'::uuid, 'dab46e5c-628a-4360-ad1d-3aaba61768f0'::uuid, 'Blanked 2026-10-07. 🔴🔴 THE MEMBER WAS NOT IN THE LEGISLATURE WHEN THE CLAIMED VOTE HAPPENED. William F. MacGregor was not in the legislature when the ROE Act was voted on: not a member of the 191 General Court, first served in the 193. The claim is impossible, not merely unsupported. The sponsorship limb was also checked: William F. MacGregor is on none of 191/H3320. 🔴 THE CITED BILL IS NOT THE ACT. The row cites 192/H3320, which is "An Act establishing the GREEN Initiative". The ROE Act''s own bill, H.3320 of the 191st, NEVER REACHED A FLOOR VOTE -- "No further action taken", 1/5/2021. The ROE Act became law as H.5179, "An Act providing for access to reproductive health services", enacted as section 40 of the FY21 budget and passed over the Governor''s veto: Chapter 263 of the Acts of 2020. 🔑 CHECK TENURE BEFORE READING A VOTE OR A NON-VOTE -- the rule from the Texas SB 17 pass, which cost two wrong blanks there. ⚠ AND CHECK IT IN BOTH BRANCHES: a profile page lists only the courts served in THAT chamber, so eighteen members of this cohort have a second profile for their earlier House career. Three rows were rescued from this very verdict that way, and this one was tested against both. The sources examined are kept below so the next reader does not re-derive this. This is a blank, not a deletion -- the chair may well be re-researchable, and that is an invitation.', ARRAY['https://malegislature.gov/Bills/192/H3320', 'https://malegislature.gov/Legislators/Profile/WFM1']::text[]),
  -- William J. Driscoll / voting-rights  (Season 1 chair 2 -> 0, LADDER_SCOPE)
    ('ab975fdf-b4f1-4955-94a4-97681a2a8d08'::uuid, 'd1792200-1d3b-4955-a0b7-0e6980d7a7b2'::uuid, '86d893a1-c1a2-4bbf-b4e5-69ec43221194'::uuid, '2a18c152-67a0-4380-a381-cb8795110a7c'::uuid, 'Blanked 2026-10-07, and ⚠ THE UNDERLYING FINDING IS TRUE -- it is recorded here so it is not lost. William J. Driscoll voted for the VOTES Act -- House roll call #200 (enactment, 06/16/2022), 126-29. The vote was divided (81% yea), so it is distinctive; only the citation was false. The Season 2 rung at this value asks a different question. Season 1: "expand early voting periods and make mail-in voting available to all voters without requiring an excuse" Season 2: "Accept non-photo identification, such as a utility bill or bank statement." The finding itself stands and is preserved here, but it cannot seat the Season 2 chair, and a repair may not move a chair. (the parse was checked against the roll call''s own declared totals before any name was read off it). 🔴 THE CITED BILL IS NOT THE ACT. The row cites 192/S2294, which is "An Act relative to tolls on the roadways of the Commonwealth". The VOTES Act was filed as S.2545, reprinted as S.2554 and ENACTED AS S.2924, Chapter 92 of the Acts of 2022. 🔴🔴 BUT THE SEASON 2 LADDER ASKS A DIFFERENT QUESTION. The Season 2 rung at this value asks a different question. Season 1: "expand early voting periods and make mail-in voting available to all voters without requiring an excuse" Season 2: "Accept non-photo identification, such as a utility bill or bank statement." Season 1 asked about registration, early voting and mail ballots -- the subject of the VOTES Act. Season 2 asks only about VOTER IDENTIFICATION. A verified vote on the VOTES Act locates nobody on a voter-ID scale, so carrying the chair across would seat this member on a position never assessed. That is the Carson call of migration 1896 and the ladder-scope register. A verified fact with nowhere to sit is still a verified fact: it is written here so the next researcher starts from it rather than from nothing. The sources examined are kept below so the next reader does not re-derive this. This is a blank, not a deletion -- the chair may well be re-researchable, and that is an invitation.', ARRAY['https://malegislature.gov/Bills/192/S2294', 'https://malegislature.gov/Bills/192/S2924', 'https://malegislature.gov/RollCall/192/HouseRollCall200.pdf']::text[]);

