UPDATE inform.politician_context SET reasoning = 'Citation repaired 2026-10-07 (migration 1900); THE CHAIR IS UNCHANGED. The claim was right and the citation was wrong. 🔴 THE CITED BILL IS NOT THE ACT. The row cites 194/H5034, which is "An Act relative to waiving the maximum age requirement for police officers for Matthew Cummings". The Affordable Homes Act is H.4977, Chapter 150 of the Acts of 2024 -- the one act in this cohort whose familiar number IS the enacted vehicle. 🔑 THE VOTE IS VERIFIED AGAINST THE PRIMARY RECORD: Brian W. Murray voted for the Affordable Homes Act -- House roll call #199 (enactment, 08/01/2024), 128-24. The vote was divided (84% yea), so it is distinctive; only the citation was false. (the parse was checked against the roll call''s own declared totals before any name was read off it). 🔑 A near-unanimous vote cannot establish a distinctive position -- the rule that blanked Newhouse on 385-41 in migration 1894 and Dingell on 417-10 in 1896 -- so the margin was checked before the chair was kept, not after. The sources now point at the enacted vehicle and the roll call itself.', sources = ARRAY['https://malegislature.gov/Bills/193/H4977', 'https://malegislature.gov/Legislators/Profile/BWM1/Bills', 'https://malegislature.gov/RollCall/193/HouseRollCall199.pdf']::text[], updated_at = now()
